1 _DSCR The Anglo-Saxon name Cockshott comes from when the family resided in Cockshut, a small chapelry in the county of Salop.   This distinguished name is derived from the Old English word of "Coccscyute", which when translated means the place where the
2 CONC y stretched the nets to catch a small game bird called a woodcock.  First found in Sussex, where they were seated from ancient times.
