2 TITL Tristram Coffin Medal
1 _OID 8b7c0df9-28e6-4e15-bcfd-fc0806278dbc
1 DATE ca. 1990's
1 _DSCR The Coffin medal, a coin with a likeness of Tristram Coffin, dated 1642, imprinted with the following: Tristram Coffin, The First of His Race That Settled in America. First Chief Magistrate of Nantucket, 1671. Attached paper says " Tristram Coffy
2 CONC n First Chief Magistrate of the Islands of Nantuckett and Tuckanuckett, June 29th 1671". Tristram Coffin was born in 1605, Brixton, Devonshire County, England. Married Dionis Stevens about 1630. Emigrated to America in 1642, with his wife, five chi
2 CONC ldren, his widowed mother, and two unmarried sisters. He first came to Nantucket in 1659 as one of nine men who purchased the island from Thomas Mayhew and son. He was, in fact, the second Chief Magistrate of Nantucket, succeeding Thomas Macy in 16
2 CONC 77. He died in Nantucket, in 1681, at age 76.  Nantucket Historical Association. CD#87
1 _CREA 2024-07-14 04:16:24.582
