2 TITL Kingsbury House (1660) 52 High St., Ipswich, MA
1 _OID 8e058534-ba90-48f9-80e9-7c16683a944a
1 _DSCR The Kingsbury House. (1660) 52 High Street. On 8 Feb 1648 he sold his farm in Ipswich, 32 acres, for 5 pounds to Thomas Safford, and that same year he bought from Daniel Ladd of Haverhill "house and land on High St. in Ipswich". The house stood a
2 CONC t the north corner, on "the street or lane leading into the Mill St. southeast". His house was later numbered 52 High Street. While Henry lived there, the green logs that formed the great fireplace in his High Street home ignited, causing considera
2 CONC ble damage to his house. Soon after, Henry began to operate a brick kiln, the first one in Ipswich. -- While Henry Kingsbury was the original owner of this house, it is another example of a house that was owned for many years by the Lord family. A
2 CONC t one time, the house was owned by 3 different people.
